course: dictionary
lesson: 4204
title: Gory and the gory details
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something feels as well as what it is. «Pretending you are not scared is very common, and many people cover their eyes at gory bits.» The words cover their eyes show that the bits are frightening or upsetting to watch. So gory bits must be parts with a lot of blood and violence.
explain: «It was gorier than any of them expected.» The -ier ending means more, so gorier means more full of blood and violence than something else. Check by swapping in your meaning: "It was more full of blood and violence than any of them expected." That still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: In everyday talk, people sometimes say «the gory details» as a joke. It means every unpleasant or embarrassing bit of a story, told in full. If a friend says, «Tell me all the gory details!», they want everything, even the parts you would rather skip.
fact: Gory means full of blood and violence, often in a film, game or story.
fact: «Gory» can be used for a film, a game or a story: «a gory film».
fact: Gory has comparative and superlative forms: gorier means more gory, and goriest means the most gory.
fact: The noun gore means blood, especially from a wound.
fact: Informal: «the gory details» means the unpleasant or embarrassing details of something, told fully.
exercise: «It was gorier than any of them expected.» What does gorier mean? | Smaller and quieter | Happier and brighter | Shorter and funnier | *More full of blood and violence
exercise: Tom says the film was gory. What does gory mean? | Full of songs and dancing | Full of cold, grey weather | *Full of blood and violence | Full of new and clever ideas
exercise: Ella asks, «Tell me all the gory details!» What does Ella want? | *Every unpleasant or embarrassing detail, told in full | A gift wrapped in gold paper | A short picture of the day | A list of the best places to eat
test: «Many people cover their eyes at gory bits.» Find and copy the word that tells you the bits are scary or upsetting. | people | bits | *cover | many
test: Which word is the noun form of gory, meaning blood? | gory bits | gorier | *gore | goriest
exam: Which word means the most full of blood and violence? | gore | gorier | gory details | *goriest
